  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the value of $x_{2007}$ given the recurrence relation $x_{n+3}x_n = x_{n+2} + x_{n+1}$ with initial conditions $x_1 = x_2 = x_3 = 1$.\n\nFirst, let's compute the first few terms of the sequence to identify any patterns.\n\nFor $n=1$:\n\\[\nx_4x_1 = x_3 + x_2 \\implies x_4 \\cdot 1 = 1 + 1 \\implies x_4 = 2\n\\]\n\nFor $n=2$:\n\\[\nx_5x_2 = x_4 + x_3 \\implies x_5 \\cdot 1 = 2 + 1 \\implies x_5 = 3\n\\]\n\nFor $n=3$:\n\\[\nx_6x_3 = x_5 + x_4 \\implies x_6 \\cdot 1 = 3 + 2 \\implies x_6 = 5\n\\]\n\nFor $n=4$:\n\\[\nx_7x_4 = x_6 + x_5 \\implies x_7 \\cdot 2 = 5 + 3 \\implies x_7 = 4\n\\]\n\nFor $n=5$:\n\\[\nx_8x_5 = x_7 + x_6 \\implies x_8 \\cdot 3 = 4 + 5 \\implies x_8 = 3\n\\]\n\nFor $n=6$:\n\\[\nx_9x_6 = x_8 + x_7 \\implies x_9 \\cdot 5 = 3 + 4 \\implies x_9 = 1\n\\]\n\nFor $n=7$:\n\\[\nx_{10}x_7 = x_9 + x_8 \\implies x_{10} \\cdot 4 = 1 + 3 \\implies x_{10} = 1\n\\]\n\nFor $n=8$:\n\\[\nx_{11}x_8 = x_9 + x_{10} \\implies x_{11} \\cdot 3 = 1 + 1 \\implies x_{11} = 2\n\\]\n\nFor $n=9$:\n\\[\nx_{12}x_9 = x_{10} + x_{11} \\implies x_{12} \\cdot 1 = 1 + 2 \\implies x_{12} = 3\n\\]\n\nFor $n=10$:\n\\[\nx_{13}x_{10} = x_{11} + x_{12} \\implies x_{13} \\cdot 1 = 2 + 3 \\implies x_{13} = 5\n\\]\n\nWe observe that the sequence repeats every 12 terms: $1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 4, 3, 1, 1, 2, 3, \\ldots$. Therefore, $x_{2007} = x_{2007 \\mod 12}$.\n\nSince $2007 \\mod 12 = 3$, we have $x_{2007} = x_3 = 1$.\n\nThus, the final answer is $\\boxed{1}$.",
